This repo follows the agent conventions in [agents/CONTEXT.md](../../agents/CONTEXT.md) — read
it first for root-finding (locate `config.json` + sibling `engine/build_cv.py`; if missing, run
`python scripts/init_workspace.py`), which files an agent may write, and the never-auto-commit
rule.

For setting up or evolving CV content (`profile/background.md`, and two masters —
`master/master_cv.md` the primary/complete inventory, `master/master_cv_minimal.md` its
condensation), follow [agents/cv-setup.md](../../agents/cv-setup.md).

For tailoring a CV to a specific posting — scan, draft, build, validate, render, and stage,
plus an optional cover letter — follow [agents/cv-tailor.md](../../agents/cv-tailor.md).

For prepping and rehearsing an upcoming interview for an application already in this root —
follow [agents/interview-prep.md](../../agents/interview-prep.md).

For the `application.md`/template/master format contract, see
[docs/SPEC.md](../../docs/SPEC.md). For `config.json`, see
[docs/CONFIG.md](../../docs/CONFIG.md). For which file to edit — content, structure, or the
PDF's visual look — see [docs/CUSTOMIZING.md](../../docs/CUSTOMIZING.md).

Working on this repo itself rather than a user's CV content? See
[community/README.md](../../community/README.md) — never open, label, or close a GitHub issue
without the maintainer's explicit approval first.

This file is a pointer, not a copy — if it looks stale, the files above are the source of truth.
